// REJECTS: Column data type VARCHAR requires 1 parameter (size)
//
// The grammar makes the parameter list optional for EVERY column type -- one rule,
// `(PAREN_OPEN INTEGER (COMMA INTEGER)? PAREN_CLOSE)?`, shared by all of them. Which types
// require parameters, and how many, is decided afterwards in the WALKER, type by type.
//
// So a parser generated straight from the .g4 accepts a bare VARCHAR and builds a column
// with no size. Nothing downstream re-checks it. This is the arity half of the rule; the
// paramless half is in neg-relational-integer-with-size.pure.
###Relational
Database fixture::neg::VarcharNoSize
(
   Table T (ID VARCHAR PRIMARY KEY)
)
